,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Both the read chokepoint (_reads._tracker) and the write guard (event_prepare._ensure_initialized) call it, so read and write agree on store usability.'","Plan: '.env-id is NOT used as a predicate (it is git-ignored local state, absent right after a valid clone).'","Closed ticket ab61 completion note: 'The gate is enforced once at src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py ... inside append_event(). Every write command ... routes through this single seam.'","src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:555 comment: 'Init gate at the single write seam (bug roar-nurse-stomp) ... enforcing .env-id once keeps the precondition consistent across ALL write commands.'"],"finding":"The plan's central rationale — 'Both the read chokepoint and the write guard call [the shared predicate], so read and write agree on store usability' — is measured against `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` (a `.git`-presence check), but the AUTHORITATIVE write init gate is now `_seam.append_event`, which enforces `.env-id` (per the plan's own cited closed ticket ab61-f3e8-6ee6-4905, seen at `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:555`). Because the plan deliberately rejects `.env-id` as the read predicate, right after a valid clone (HEAD resolves, `.env-id` not yet written) reads will report the store USABLE while the effective write path still rejects it as 'not initialized' — so read and write do NOT actually agree, contrary to the stated design goal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4133576a4e71acc0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> Design / 'Caller-dependency gate' / 'Approved change'","norm_id":"n8f1d6494e659c371","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A tracker freshly cloned by the entrypoint (HEAD resolvable) but before .env-id is regenerated: reads answer normally while any write (comment/create) fails 'not initialized' — the exact read/write disagreement the plan claims to eliminate."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State explicitly that reads gate on store USABILITY (`.git`+HEAD) while writes additionally require local `.env-id` initialization, and argue why that asymmetry is intended (a cloned-but-not-locally-initialized store is legitimately readable). If instead full parity is the goal, have the shared predicate also drive `_seam.append_event`, or add an AC covering the freshly-cloned, `.env-id`-absent state so the residual disagreement is not silently shipped.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the .env-id discussion: the Constraint section still frames .env-id as the likely marker while the Fix plan rejects it — align both sections on the final predicate (.git + resolvable HEAD, no .env-id).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["COH","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6868,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'It has to be \"is this a usable store\": rebar's own `.env-id` initialization marker and/or a resolvable git HEAD ... suggests `.env-id` is the intended marker.'","'`.env-id` is NOT used as a predicate (it is git-ignored local state, absent right after a valid clone).'"],"finding":"The problem-framing 'Constraint' section proposes the discriminator could be \".env-id ... and/or a resolvable git HEAD\" and cites ab61 as evidence \".env-id is the intended marker\", while the approved Fix plan explicitly states \".env-id is NOT used as a predicate\". The two sections point an implementer in opposite directions on the marker.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5010e7797c03ab75","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraint the fix must respect / Approved change","norm_id":"na6a3904741514695","priority":0.1132,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line note in the Constraint section that the approved predicate is `.git present AND HEAD resolves` and .env-id was rejected because it is git-ignored local state absent right after a valid clone.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reference the existing HEAD-resolution predicates (sync._ok / init._git_ok) and the worktree-aware .git resolution (gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir / paths.git_dir) when specifying store_is_usable, and state why a fresh stdlib-only subprocess is preferred over reusing gitutil.run_git given the import-SCC constraint — and confirm the '.git present' check handles .git-as-FILE (linked worktree), not just .git-as-dir.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8714,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Predicate: .git present AND git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD resolves'","Existing: src/rebar/_store/sync.py:129 `if not _ok(tracker, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"HEAD\")`","Existing: src/rebar/_commands/init.py:165 `_git_ok(tracker, \"rev-parse\", \"--is-inside-work-tree\")`","Existing worktree-aware .git resolution: src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:72 `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` handles `.git` as FILE (gitdir: pointer) and as directory; src/rebar/_store/paths.py:145 `git_dir` property does the same","gitutil module docstring: 'consolidates the dozen hand-rolled _git() wrappers that had drifted into a different signature/return/error contract each' (src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:4-10) — the canonical wrapper the new leaf's subprocess call risks re-forking"],"finding":"The new store_is_usable leaf reimplements a HEAD-resolution predicate that already exists (sync._ok 'rev-parse --verify HEAD'; init._git_ok 'rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree') and a '.git present' check that gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir / paths.git_dir already implement — including the linked-worktree case where <tracker>/.git is a FILE (gitdir: pointer), not a directory. The plan's predicate ('.git present' via os.path.exists is fine, but the surrounding rationale) does not acknowledge these existing implementations or the worktree nuance, risking either silent divergence from the established predicates or misjudging a valid linked-worktree store as unusable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff8bed5920e7216bc","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> Design / Files: src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py (new)","norm_id":"n67a7ebe6ec122f86","priority":0.0786,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store is a linked worktree/submodule where <tracker>/.git is a FILE, not a dir: a naive os.path.isdir(.git) check would call it unusable and wrongly raise store_uninitialized on a valid store","The new leaf's HEAD predicate drifts from sync/_ok semantics over time, so read-usability and sync-usability disagree again — the exact read/write disagreement this plan sets out to eliminate"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the Design section, note that store_is_usable's HEAD check mirrors sync._ok('rev-parse','--verify','HEAD') and its .git-presence check must accept a .git FILE (gitdir: pointer) as gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir/paths.git_dir already do, so a linked-worktree store is not misjudged unusable; justify the stdlib-only re-implementation explicitly against the import-SCC constraint rather than leaving the duplication implicit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the non-audit consumers of the 7 affected read entry points (rebar._reads importers in _lib_reads.py, llm/*, _commands/*, and rebar.list_tickets in _mcp_reads.py) and confirm none relied on []-for-present-but-broken-store, rather than backing the 'no caller depends' claim only with the single store_uninitialized-catching audit consumer.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Only rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets consumes store_uninitialized ... No caller depends on the old []-for-broken-store.'","Grep 'from rebar import _reads' returns src/rebar/_lib_reads.py, src/rebar/llm/completion.py, src/rebar/llm/enrich.py, src/rebar/llm/operations.py, src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py, and many more.","src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:311 calls rebar.list_tickets(...).","Mitigating fact: the ABSENT-store store_uninitialized raise already shipped (CHANGELOG.md:38-45), so consumers already tolerate the raise; only the present-but-broken case is newly affected."],"finding":"The caller-dependency gate asserts 'No caller depends on the old []-for-broken-store' but enumerates only rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets (the sole store_uninitialized-catching consumer), while many other modules consume the affected read entry points (rebar._reads is imported by src/rebar/_lib_reads.py, numerous src/rebar/llm/* modules, src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py, and rebar.list_tickets by src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py). These are outside the artifact dir and their behavior changes for a present-but-unusable store (now raises instead of []). The gate does not enumerate this broader consumer set to justify the 'no caller depends' claim.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa6dc9954ac90f98d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Caller-dependency gate' section","norm_id":"nfa5b60f00d011c03","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A read consumer in llm/* or _commands/* that today silently gets [] from a present-but-broken store (e.g. mid-clone) and proceeds, now sees a RebarError propagate."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short sweep noting that the ABSENT-store store_uninitialized raise already shipped (so consumers already tolerate the raise) and that the only newly-affected path is present-but-unusable stores; then confirm no read consumer branches on [] specifically for that case.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4444,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"ab100e3a31596788","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["d45295face4dc132",5673],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["fe24fbca94f308ef",4],"ticket_id":["d0b409b5babd3489",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-net